;;; The twin of `rung-unactivated.ein` that is not wrong — **W97**, register
;;; row `W97/unactivated`'s twin (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;;
;;; The same program with the obligation stated: `(total-owed at is-a)`
;;; activates `std.algebra`'s `total-owed` over `at`, and Red, the one
;;; colour, has a house, so root owes nothing. An obligation activated at root
;;; takes the ladder's second rung, and a discharged state under it proposes
;;; nothing and is complete: no candidate, and R is {∅}, one state. `near`,
;;; which nothing owes, is the read-out's `outside` row. This is the answer
;;; with the rung chosen by an obligation activated, as it was with the rung
;;; chosen by an obligation rule loaded: the ruling does not move it.

(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed))
(relation at Color House :why "{?1} is at {?2}")
(relation near House House :why "{?1} is near {?2}")
(is-a Red Color) (is-a H1 House) (is-a H2 House)
(total-owed at is-a)
(at Red H1)
(solve)
